<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="62127" href="schedule/2015/spring/ARTS/499/62127.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2015" href="schedule/2015.xml">2015</calendarYear><term id="120151" href="schedule/2015/spring.xml">Spring 2015</term><subject id="ARTS" href="schedule/2015/spring/ARTS.xml">Art--Studio</subject><course id="499" href="schedule/2015/spring/ARTS/499.xml">Special Topics in Studio Art</course></parents><sectionNumber>G  </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Lithography &amp; Screenprint</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic: Lithography and Screenprint.  Students will learn basic techniques of lithography and screenprint, with an emphasis on relationships between processes, materials and aesthetics.  Both traditional and digital techniques will be explored, and projects that relate to work developed in other studio and design areas will be encouraged.  This course features hands-on making combined with discussion of the historical arc of printmaking and unique conceptual concerns of print media.  Graduate Section.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Closed</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2015-01-20Z</startDate><endDate>2015-05-06Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LAB">Laboratory</type><start>05:00 PM</start><end>07:40 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>7</roomNumber><buildingName>Noble Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Lingscheit" firstName="E">Lingscheit, E</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>